# Tracer: recursive object resolution retains a replayable source-to-goal proof.
#
# Before (Litex verified, but generated Lean did not type-check):
# abstract_prop p(x)
#
# forall a, b R:
#     a = 13
#     b = 1
#     $p(14)
#     =>:
#         $p(a + b)
#
# Former behavior: the atomic-fact lookup resolved `a + b` to `14`, found the
# stored `$p(14)`, and then returned only that citation. To-Lean consequently
# emitted an `exact` proof of `$p(14)` at the different goal `$p(a + b)`.
#
# Now (verified and compiled from explicit transformations):
abstract_prop p(x)

forall a, b R:
    a = 13
    b = 1
    $p(14)
    =>:
        $p(a + b)

# Current behavior: verification searches from the requested goal to the
# stored source, but records the successful proof in construction order:
#
#     $p(14)
#       -- RationalNormalization --> $p(13 + 1)
#       -- EqualityRewrite[a = 13, b = 1] --> $p(a + b)
#
# Each equality rewrite retains its stored FactId. To-Lean lowers both steps as
# nested RuleApplication nodes and emits a checked `convert` followed by
# `simpa only` over the two named equality proofs. It does not rerun resolve.
#
# Recursive boundary check: the same verifier evidence builder descends through
# every supported Obj shape. The focused Rust regression confirms that
# `$p(f(14), c)` becomes `$p(f(13 + 1), c)` and then `$p(f(a + b), c)`.
# General function objects still lack a To-Lean Obj ABI, so compiling that
# second source remains an explicit `FnSet object` boundary rather than an
# axiom, `sorry`, or flattened citation.
#
# Evidence: target/release/litex -compact -isolated -runner -f examples/05_compiler_interop/to_lean_resolved_atomic_fact.lit
# Compiler evidence: cargo test --release resolved_atomic_fact -- --nocapture
# Lean kernel evidence: LITEX_LEAN_PROJECT=<mathlib-project> LITEX_LAKE=<lake-path> cargo test --release generated_to_lean_resolved_atomic_fact_compiles_with_lean -- --ignored --nocapture
# Implementation: src/verify/verify_known_atomic_facts.rs,
# src/result/runtime_success.rs, src/runtime/runtime_to_lean_ir.rs,
# src/to_lean/to_lean_pipeline.rs
